  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be the solution curve of the differential equation, <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> , satisfying <math><mi>y</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> . This curve intersects the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis at a point whose abscissa is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mo>-</mo><mi>e</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
